WEBVTT

00:41.333 --> 00:43.961
NO TAIL TO TELL

00:45.254 --> 00:46.129
Anyway…

00:46.213 --> 00:47.172
I WILL GRANT YOUR WISH

00:47.965 --> 00:48.882
…what's this?

00:49.466 --> 00:50.467
Oh, that.

00:52.177 --> 00:53.136
Hey, Woo-seok.

00:54.012 --> 00:55.180
By any chance,

00:56.181 --> 00:57.224
do you have a wish?

00:59.893 --> 01:00.894
A wish?

01:04.940 --> 01:06.942
Why? Are you going to grant it?

01:07.859 --> 01:09.486
No, it's not that. Actually--

01:09.570 --> 01:12.614
It's fine.
It's my life, so I'll handle it myself.

01:12.698 --> 01:14.324
I should get going now, Si-yeol.

01:17.411 --> 01:18.412
By the way…

01:23.750 --> 01:25.586
Congrats on the contract renewal.

01:27.004 --> 01:28.505
Hey…

01:48.984 --> 01:51.236
- Hey, Yeon-su.
- Si-yeol, we've got a problem.

01:51.862 --> 01:52.904
Now what?

01:52.988 --> 01:54.573
What's all the fuss about?

01:54.656 --> 01:56.283
Thames FC is facing relegation.

01:56.366 --> 01:58.535
What on earth are you talking about?

01:59.244 --> 02:01.622
Relegation? We won the league last season.

02:02.497 --> 02:06.001
They're voiding last season's title,
stripping us of our Champions League spot,

02:06.084 --> 02:08.253
and relegating us to the Championship.

02:09.963 --> 02:11.214
Is it April Fools' Day?

02:11.298 --> 02:12.716
I'm serious.

02:12.799 --> 02:15.260
Apparently, Thames violated
Financial Fair Play regulations,

02:15.344 --> 02:18.388
so UEFA just slapped them with sanctions.

02:24.186 --> 02:25.854
Explain it in simple terms.

02:25.937 --> 02:27.856
What exactly is "Financial Fair Play"?

02:27.939 --> 02:29.399
It's a UEFA rule stating

02:29.483 --> 02:33.779
that a club can't spend more than
a certain percentage of its revenue.

02:33.862 --> 02:35.864
I still don't get it.

02:36.657 --> 02:39.743
Basically, the club
committed accounting fraud

02:40.369 --> 02:42.913
to cover your transfer fee
and massive salary.

02:45.123 --> 02:47.334
So what am I supposed to do now?

02:48.126 --> 02:49.628
Will you play in the second division?

02:49.711 --> 02:51.922
Are you crazy? I'm Kang Si-yeol.

02:53.215 --> 02:55.133
Then there's only one option left.

04:01.658 --> 04:03.410
What the…

04:04.828 --> 04:05.704
KANG SI-YEOL

04:05.787 --> 04:08.415
THAMES FC REFUSES TRANSFER
KANG SI-YEOL FACES A MAJOR CRISIS

04:13.628 --> 04:15.088
SECOND DIVISION NEXT FOR KANG SI-YEOL?

04:16.715 --> 04:18.508
THAMES FC CHARGED
WITH VIOLATING FFP REGULATIONS

04:27.267 --> 04:28.268
This won't do.

04:29.478 --> 04:30.771
Your passport's at home, right?

04:30.854 --> 04:32.397
I'll have someone bring it over.

04:32.481 --> 04:34.316
Let's head to the airport right now.

04:34.399 --> 04:37.110
I don't think staying in Korea
will solve anything.

04:37.194 --> 04:40.238
Okay, find the earliest flight
available right now.

04:46.286 --> 04:48.121
What are you doing? Let's hurry.

04:49.372 --> 04:50.540
Yeah, I'm coming.

04:53.293 --> 04:55.128
NOVEMBER 20TH
ANNIVERSARY OF GRANDMA'S DEATH

04:58.507 --> 05:03.470
DEACON KIM BOK-SUN
MAY SHE REST IN PEACE

05:05.555 --> 05:06.598
Ms. Kim.

05:09.100 --> 05:12.938
It didn't look like Si-yeol would make it
again this year, so I came instead.

05:14.648 --> 05:18.235
Gosh, you know how busy he is.

05:19.694 --> 05:22.614
Still, seeing how he timed his return,

05:22.697 --> 05:25.116
it seems like he really meant
to come this year.

05:26.785 --> 05:28.578
But something came up,

05:28.662 --> 05:30.914
so he's probably
out of the country right now.

05:45.637 --> 05:47.138
Hey, you…

05:48.265 --> 05:51.017
Grandma, I'm here.

05:54.896 --> 05:59.234
Looks like Woo-seok's been coming
to see you, Grandma.

05:59.985 --> 06:01.903
He won't even see me these days.

06:23.925 --> 06:26.469
GARDEN OF PEACE MEMORIAL PARK

06:26.553 --> 06:27.721
I know

06:28.972 --> 06:31.266
you looked after my grandma for me,

06:31.892 --> 06:35.770
visiting her every holiday
and taking her to the hospital.

06:36.813 --> 06:40.025
That's because you were abroad.

06:41.860 --> 06:43.904
You were there when she passed too.

06:44.738 --> 06:48.408
And you've been bringing her flowers
every year on her anniversary.

06:48.491 --> 06:51.536
Hey, why are you getting all sappy?

06:53.371 --> 06:55.957
That's the kind of friend you are to me.

06:56.041 --> 06:58.752
You can tell me anything, okay?

06:58.835 --> 07:01.421
If you ever need help, I've got your back.

07:01.922 --> 07:03.965
If you need money, I can give you--

07:04.049 --> 07:06.343
That's why I'm avoiding you right now.

07:11.514 --> 07:12.849
I don't want…

07:14.184 --> 07:17.812
to ask you for favors
or borrow money from you.

07:18.939 --> 07:21.232
I want us to stay friends.

07:21.900 --> 07:23.902
Even if you're a Premier League player,

07:24.736 --> 07:27.030
no matter how famous you are,

07:28.198 --> 07:30.825
I want us to be friends for who we are.

07:32.577 --> 07:35.997
But if I start asking you for things
or relying on you for help,

07:36.081 --> 07:38.833
I wouldn't be able to see you
as a friend anymore.

07:42.545 --> 07:44.798
- Woo-seok--
- Let's stop talking about this.

07:44.881 --> 07:46.132
Just think of it

07:47.217 --> 07:49.386
as giving me some space for now.

07:53.223 --> 07:54.265
But seriously,

07:55.016 --> 07:57.185
is it really okay for you to be here?

08:00.230 --> 08:02.857
Actually, my agent's already in the UK.

08:03.525 --> 08:06.319
I said I'd stop by my grandma's grave,
then head there right away.

08:07.320 --> 08:09.114
Do you think things will work out?

08:10.657 --> 08:12.367
It doesn't look good right now.

08:12.450 --> 08:15.495
The only option is to meet
and convince them,

08:16.371 --> 08:19.541
but neither the chairman
nor the coach will see my agent.

08:24.629 --> 08:26.256
Jeez, another reporter.

08:26.339 --> 08:27.716
I'd better go.

08:27.799 --> 08:29.884
I should go see what I can do.

08:29.968 --> 08:30.969
Hey, wait.

08:32.345 --> 08:33.471
You dropped this.

08:34.889 --> 08:35.765
What is this?

08:35.849 --> 08:36.808
I WILL GRANT YOUR WISH

08:36.891 --> 08:38.727
Are you into this kind of stuff lately?

08:38.810 --> 08:40.645
Isn't this like a cult or something?

08:41.771 --> 08:42.647
Oh, right.

08:46.860 --> 08:47.777
Woo-seok.

08:49.946 --> 08:51.114
I think…

08:52.866 --> 08:54.534
there might be a way.

09:02.292 --> 09:04.627
The player is determined to transfer.

09:04.711 --> 09:07.422
But Thames FC is refusing
to negotiate at all.

09:07.505 --> 09:10.050
We offered
a 180 million euro transfer fee,

09:10.675 --> 09:13.845
but they reiterated
that he isn't for sale.

09:18.808 --> 09:21.436
I WILL GRANT YOUR WISH

09:22.312 --> 09:24.272
Hey, what are you doing? That's dangerous.

09:25.356 --> 09:28.526
I'm pretty sure
this is how I was told to do it.

09:36.701 --> 09:37.869
Are you okay?

09:38.995 --> 09:40.205
Why isn't it working?

10:08.066 --> 10:10.652
You summoned me sooner
than I expected, Si-yeol.

10:10.735 --> 10:13.988
Then again, the more humans have,

10:14.072 --> 10:17.534
the greedier they get,
and the bigger their worries become.

10:18.201 --> 10:21.121
That's why they always end up
needing beings like me.

10:23.540 --> 10:25.500
So, tell me.

10:26.334 --> 10:28.086
What's this great wish of yours?

10:41.599 --> 10:45.687
EPISODE 3
THE RISE AND FALL

10:47.772 --> 10:50.525
THAMES FC, LONDON, UK

10:59.951 --> 11:01.578
That's none of your business.

11:05.373 --> 11:07.292
I heard there's a nice pub nearby.

11:07.375 --> 11:10.170
If you're done for the day,
why don't you stop by?

11:33.067 --> 11:35.028
I couldn't even get him to see me,

11:35.778 --> 11:37.739
and now I just run into him here?

11:56.299 --> 11:57.425
So,

11:58.760 --> 12:02.222
the real reason the Geumsu Group heir
turned himself in nine years ago

12:02.931 --> 12:04.974
was because of that person… I mean…

12:05.058 --> 12:06.059
Nine-tailed fox.

12:06.559 --> 12:07.435
Right.

12:08.811 --> 12:10.772
It was because of that nine-tailed fox?

12:12.106 --> 12:13.024
Yeah.

12:13.900 --> 12:16.986
I can't believe it,
but I can't say I don't believe it either.

12:18.404 --> 12:20.490
But still,

12:21.032 --> 12:23.576
she said she'd grant your wish,
and that's it?

12:23.660 --> 12:26.037
She just listened and disappeared.

12:26.120 --> 12:28.873
I know.
I'm not sure what's going on either.

12:32.335 --> 12:33.378
RECENT WITHDRAWALS

12:34.212 --> 12:35.088
What the…

12:36.798 --> 12:37.674
What is it?

12:38.216 --> 12:40.301
Did she really fix things?

12:40.385 --> 12:43.221
No, but money was taken out of my account.

12:43.304 --> 12:45.098
Out of the blue? How much?

12:46.140 --> 12:48.059
- One hundred million won.
- What?

12:51.521 --> 12:53.398
What the hell?

12:53.481 --> 12:56.609
Hey, is your account
still getting drained?

12:57.568 --> 12:59.112
Could it be a phone scam?

13:08.204 --> 13:09.539
Hello?

13:10.039 --> 13:13.251
Si-yeol, it's all settled.
You're clear for the transfer.

13:13.876 --> 13:14.836
Really?

13:14.919 --> 13:19.590
Yeah. I just ran into the chairman,
and it was like he was possessed.

13:19.674 --> 13:23.136
He agreed to your transfer
and wants to know your preferred team.

13:23.219 --> 13:25.763
He said he'll give
your negotiations top priority.

13:32.937 --> 13:34.772
What did she say?

13:36.357 --> 13:37.650
So can you transfer?

13:43.072 --> 13:43.948
Really?

13:44.699 --> 13:47.493
It's settled? Just like that?

13:48.369 --> 13:49.245
Yeah.

13:50.455 --> 13:51.789
Just like that.

14:06.012 --> 14:07.847
- Hey, that's Kang Si-yeol.
- Hello.

14:07.930 --> 14:08.973
Hello.

14:19.609 --> 14:20.526
Si-yeol!

14:24.280 --> 14:25.281
Hey, Woo-seok.

14:26.908 --> 14:28.368
What are you doing here?

14:29.911 --> 14:32.705
Si-yeol, can I really

14:34.040 --> 14:36.417
ask you for a favor?

14:37.752 --> 14:38.628
Of course.

14:39.754 --> 14:42.840
The truth is,
I don't want to quit like this.

14:44.008 --> 14:45.968
I want to play professionally,

14:46.594 --> 14:49.555
and I want to play
for the national team too.

14:50.306 --> 14:51.891
I really want

14:51.974 --> 14:55.269
to live my life differently, just once.

14:56.562 --> 14:57.772
Do you think…

14:58.815 --> 15:00.483
that if I made a wish like you did,

15:01.526 --> 15:02.985
it could come true?

15:08.491 --> 15:10.118
I don't think so.

15:10.201 --> 15:11.285
Why not?

15:11.953 --> 15:14.414
Wishes always come with a price.

15:14.497 --> 15:17.583
The bigger the wish,
the greater the price.

15:18.376 --> 15:19.919
But your friend here

15:21.045 --> 15:22.380
has nothing to offer.

15:24.048 --> 15:28.094
Does that price have to be money?

15:29.178 --> 15:31.806
What, are you thinking
of offering up your soul?

15:36.394 --> 15:38.896
If that's what it takes, then yes.

15:38.980 --> 15:41.315
Really? What use would that be to me?

15:42.442 --> 15:44.527
Typical humans.

15:44.610 --> 15:46.696
Always falling for tired clichés.

15:47.321 --> 15:49.365
Is there really no other way?

15:49.991 --> 15:52.702
I'll do whatever it takes.

15:55.121 --> 15:57.373
You clearly have this all wrong.

15:58.249 --> 16:01.794
You're not qualified to be my client.
Do you understand?

16:02.295 --> 16:06.007
That means that you have nothing
of any value to me.

16:06.090 --> 16:07.425
And you.

16:07.508 --> 16:09.760
You think I'm a charity or something?

16:10.720 --> 16:13.097
Don't ever summon me
for something this petty.

16:13.931 --> 16:15.224
How insolent.

16:17.185 --> 16:19.395
Don't go. We're not finished yet.

16:27.820 --> 16:28.696
What?

16:28.779 --> 16:30.990
You talk a big game,

16:31.073 --> 16:33.618
but it all comes down to money in the end.

16:34.327 --> 16:35.495
What are you getting at?

16:35.578 --> 16:38.414
I'll pay for him.
That should settle it, right?

16:40.583 --> 16:42.001
- No.
- Why not?

16:43.461 --> 16:45.671
You have to pay the price
for your own wish.

16:45.755 --> 16:49.800
But if you pay for him,
you're basically giving him your wish.

16:49.884 --> 16:51.135
What's wrong with that?

16:51.219 --> 16:54.555
What's wrong is that it's a good deed.

16:55.848 --> 16:59.101
Maybe I forgot to tell you,
but I have only one principle.

16:59.185 --> 17:02.688
I avoid doing even the smallest good deed
and only avoid doing major misdeeds.

17:02.772 --> 17:06.234
I'd hate to cultivate more virtue
and end up becoming human.

17:07.151 --> 17:09.862
Come on, stop making excuses.

17:11.197 --> 17:13.407
- Excuses?
- That sure sounds like one.

17:13.491 --> 17:16.327
You came to me first
to help catch that hit-and-run driver.

17:16.410 --> 17:18.329
If that's not a good deed, then what is?

17:18.412 --> 17:21.249
You know,
I think you'll need to make a wish.

17:21.874 --> 17:25.294
Wish for it. I'll grant it for you.

17:25.378 --> 17:27.338
What kind of principle is that, anyway?

17:28.256 --> 17:29.799
Well, that was--

17:29.882 --> 17:32.468
Just do it.
Unless it's beyond your capability.

17:36.597 --> 17:38.140
"Beyond my capability"?

17:41.811 --> 17:46.941
Come to think of it,
our first meeting was way too friendly.

17:47.024 --> 17:50.319
That's why you're being so reckless
and pushing your luck.

17:54.657 --> 17:56.617
Fine. I'll grant the wish.

17:56.701 --> 18:00.246
But how I choose to grant it is up to me.

18:00.329 --> 18:02.206
And of course, you'll pay the price.

18:03.457 --> 18:04.417
Any problems with that?

18:21.601 --> 18:23.603
I AM KANG SI-YEOL

19:39.345 --> 19:40.221
Ladies and gentlemen.

19:40.304 --> 19:42.765
We are experiencing sudden turbulence.

19:43.391 --> 19:47.019
All passengers, please remain seated
until further notice.

20:25.599 --> 20:28.394
DRIVEN BY YOUR TRUST
BEYOND SATISFACTION

20:42.575 --> 20:44.702
Wake up, you bastard!

20:49.415 --> 20:50.291
Hey!

21:02.762 --> 21:03.971
What the…

21:12.062 --> 21:13.397
Where am I?

21:37.546 --> 21:38.881
FOREVER CARE NURSING HOME

21:38.964 --> 21:40.216
What is this?

21:46.347 --> 21:47.765
Did you sleep well, Si-yeol?

21:48.557 --> 21:50.976
What's going on right now?

21:51.894 --> 21:53.771
What happened?

21:53.854 --> 21:54.939
Why am I suddenly here?

21:55.564 --> 21:58.025
You made a wish, so a price must be paid.

21:58.108 --> 21:58.984
What?

21:59.819 --> 22:01.862
Wait, what does Woo-seok's wish
have to do--

22:01.946 --> 22:03.489
Didn't I tell you?

22:03.572 --> 22:07.117
I can grant the wish,
but how I do it is up to me.

22:07.201 --> 22:09.578
Once again, your wish has been granted.

22:15.626 --> 22:18.003
What do you mean,
my wish has been granted?

22:18.671 --> 22:20.130
Where is Woo-seok right now?

22:33.227 --> 22:34.186
What?

22:39.149 --> 22:40.234
What the…

22:42.236 --> 22:43.362
Here.

22:43.904 --> 22:46.073
You dropped this, Mr. Hyeon.

22:46.156 --> 22:47.324
Oh, I see.

22:48.993 --> 22:50.911
But how do you know my name?

22:50.995 --> 22:51.996
Of course I know you.

22:52.079 --> 22:56.125
Everyone in Korea knows who you are.

22:56.208 --> 22:57.251
Right.

22:57.334 --> 22:58.294
Wait, what?

22:59.211 --> 23:00.462
What do you mean…

23:01.922 --> 23:02.798
Excuse me?

23:07.970 --> 23:09.054
What is this?

23:13.434 --> 23:14.310
"Hyeon Woo-seok."

23:15.436 --> 23:16.312
Why am I…

23:28.198 --> 23:29.992
Fine. I'll grant the wish.

23:30.075 --> 23:33.454
But how I choose to grant it is up to me.

23:37.541 --> 23:39.460
Well, let's see.

23:39.543 --> 23:42.713
Your friend is probably
where you're supposed to be right now.

23:44.757 --> 23:46.133
Oh, come on.

23:46.675 --> 23:50.179
Stop talking in riddles.
You're not making any sense.

23:50.262 --> 23:55.184
What does Woo-seok's wish have to do
with me being here?

23:56.810 --> 23:58.604
I guess it hasn't sunk in yet.

23:59.229 --> 24:00.731
That's understandable.

24:01.607 --> 24:02.691
But you know…

24:07.404 --> 24:08.906
I'm a bit busy right now.

24:08.989 --> 24:10.366
I have another client waiting.

24:10.449 --> 24:13.410
Sadly, I don't have the time
to explain everything.

24:13.494 --> 24:16.038
Are you kidding me? I was on a plane to--

24:16.121 --> 24:20.000
You'll understand exactly
what's going on soon enough.

24:20.626 --> 24:23.545
So, we'll finish this later.

24:26.799 --> 24:28.509
Jeez, what now?

24:30.386 --> 24:31.261
Wait.

24:32.096 --> 24:33.097
Where'd she go?

24:35.182 --> 24:36.684
Seriously?

24:37.518 --> 24:40.980
Hey, Si-yeol. I know you're in there!

24:41.063 --> 24:42.481
Si-yeol, open the door.

24:43.524 --> 24:45.317
- Si-yeol!
- What the hell?

24:45.401 --> 24:46.819
I know you're in there.

24:46.902 --> 24:49.446
- Open the door, Si-yeol.
- Si-yeol!

24:50.948 --> 24:52.658
See, I told you he was here.

24:52.741 --> 24:55.744
- Open the door already. Jeez.
- What took you so long?

24:55.828 --> 24:59.039
Hey, have you been drinking?

24:59.123 --> 25:00.541
- What?
- No way.

25:00.624 --> 25:02.292
You know Si-yeol doesn't drink.

25:02.376 --> 25:03.711
He's really disciplined.

25:03.794 --> 25:06.296
Look. There are empty bottles everywhere.

25:07.840 --> 25:09.675
This place is a mess.

25:10.259 --> 25:12.094
He must've been having a rough time.

25:12.594 --> 25:13.846
Hey.

25:14.471 --> 25:17.057
This is why I told you
not to let soccer consume your life.

25:17.141 --> 25:19.268
Who are you people? What is this?

25:19.351 --> 25:20.853
Do we know each other?

25:20.936 --> 25:23.480
Of course, and that's exactly why
we're here to pick you up.

25:23.564 --> 25:24.982
I've got all his things.

25:25.065 --> 25:27.151
Good. Let's go now.

25:27.234 --> 25:30.237
Go where? I'm not going anywhere!

25:30.320 --> 25:31.905
Who the hell are you guys?

25:32.781 --> 25:36.368
Why won't anyone
give me a straight answer?

25:36.452 --> 25:39.955
Si-yeol, come on. Let's go.
Just apologize to the coach.

25:40.539 --> 25:43.167
Apologize for what? To whom?

25:45.544 --> 25:47.004
Just apologize.

25:47.087 --> 25:48.756
You're such a hothead.

25:49.590 --> 25:50.549
Lift him up.

25:50.632 --> 25:51.925
- One, two, three!
- Wait, hold on!

25:52.009 --> 25:54.386
- Let's go.
- Let go of me! I said let go!

25:54.470 --> 25:56.722
Let go. Stop it!

25:56.805 --> 25:59.141
Hey, that hurts! Let me go!

25:59.224 --> 26:00.559
I'm not going anywhere!

26:10.486 --> 26:11.487
Hey.

26:15.407 --> 26:16.283
Welcome.

26:17.993 --> 26:20.871
I was wondering who it was.
It's been a while.

26:25.209 --> 26:28.629
I had this specially ordered
from the hotel patisserie.

26:29.254 --> 26:33.217
They say this is all the rage
with young people these days.

26:34.093 --> 26:35.886
I hope you like it.

26:35.969 --> 26:38.013
Gosh, you didn't have to bring anything,

26:38.097 --> 26:41.100
especially considering
how much you brought.

26:45.687 --> 26:46.563
Not bad.

26:48.565 --> 26:51.276
This is why I like familiar faces.

26:52.820 --> 26:55.447
It's just a shame
they keep dying of old age.

26:56.532 --> 26:58.784
I hope you live a long life, Chairman Kim.

26:59.827 --> 27:03.122
I guess you were taming a new client.

27:03.205 --> 27:04.248
Yes.

27:04.748 --> 27:08.043
This client is clueless and rude,

27:08.127 --> 27:10.629
so I'm taking extra care
to tame him properly.

27:15.342 --> 27:16.552
I like the scent.

27:22.099 --> 27:25.519
That fellow must be suffering quite a bit.

27:27.229 --> 27:29.481
- My gosh.
- Anyway, Chairman Kim.

27:30.190 --> 27:31.984
You've lived a long life
and have everything.

27:32.067 --> 27:33.569
And yet, you want more?

27:34.278 --> 27:36.280
You've grown greedy with age.

27:40.701 --> 27:41.869
Actually,

27:42.828 --> 27:46.999
I didn't come to see you
because I have a wish.

27:48.750 --> 27:50.085
You didn't?

27:51.211 --> 27:52.921
Then what do you want from me?

28:03.140 --> 28:04.266
Seriously.

28:05.058 --> 28:08.604
Who are you guys?
I've asked you so many times.

28:08.687 --> 28:11.023
What's with you today?

28:11.106 --> 28:12.608
Knock it off, already.

28:12.691 --> 28:14.818
You fought with the coach, not us.

28:15.736 --> 28:17.821
You can't just dump us
like a bad investment.

28:17.905 --> 28:20.532
You're not really quitting soccer
like this, are you?

28:20.616 --> 28:22.993
What are you talking about?
Why would I quit?

28:23.785 --> 28:25.204
I'm Kang Si-yeol.

28:25.287 --> 28:27.247
I know you're Kang Si-yeol.

28:27.331 --> 28:29.249
That's why we came to pick you up.

28:29.333 --> 28:31.793
What does he think he is, royalty?

28:31.877 --> 28:34.838
You'd never see a player
throw a water bottle at their coach,

28:34.922 --> 28:36.506
even in the Premier League.

28:36.590 --> 28:38.800
He didn't actually throw it at the coach.

28:38.884 --> 28:40.761
He threw it nearby,

28:40.844 --> 28:43.347
but it just bounced off the wall
and hit him, right?

28:43.430 --> 28:44.681
No way.

28:44.765 --> 28:46.642
When this jerk threw the bottle
at the coach,

28:46.725 --> 28:48.518
I saw it in his eyes. He lost it.

28:48.602 --> 28:50.103
He was aiming right at him.

28:50.187 --> 28:52.648
Come on, Si-yeol isn't that crazy.

28:52.731 --> 28:54.942
Hey! He is crazy!

28:55.025 --> 28:56.902
This is driving me crazy.

28:57.486 --> 28:58.362
Hey.

28:59.196 --> 29:00.906
Are you guys on the national team?

29:02.574 --> 29:04.493
I've never even seen any of you before.

29:05.452 --> 29:07.829
Did Coach Gonzalez tell you
to bring me in?

29:09.915 --> 29:13.168
Wow, I think he really has gone crazy.

29:13.252 --> 29:15.671
- Si-yeol.
- I told you he's crazy.

29:15.754 --> 29:16.964
Whatever, forget it.

29:17.047 --> 29:19.216
Whoever you are,
I need to get to London now.

29:19.299 --> 29:22.219
- So take me to the airport.
- London? Why?

29:22.844 --> 29:25.305
Jeez, don't you guys even watch the news?

29:26.139 --> 29:27.975
I'm in the middle
of transfer negotiations.

29:28.058 --> 29:29.017
Really?

29:29.559 --> 29:33.146
And where exactly are you transferring to?

29:33.647 --> 29:34.731
To a Sunday league team?

29:34.815 --> 29:37.025
Hey, Beom, that's a bit harsh.

29:37.109 --> 29:39.403
Si-yeol,
don't let your pride get in the way.

29:39.486 --> 29:41.571
Just go to the coach
and beg for forgiveness.

29:41.655 --> 29:43.615
- Jeez!
- Seriously!

29:43.699 --> 29:48.245
Who am I even supposed to beg,
and for what?

29:48.328 --> 29:51.039
- Oh, come on!
- Just beg.

29:51.123 --> 29:52.916
- Who am I supposed to beg?
- Knock it off.

29:53.000 --> 29:54.960
- I'm getting out!
- Hold on tight!

29:55.043 --> 29:56.211
- Stay still!
- Hold on to him!

30:20.319 --> 30:21.737
Last night,

30:22.362 --> 30:25.073
the wooden-handled dagger
that was here disappeared.

30:26.575 --> 30:32.372
I remembered you'd come by
from time to time and just stare at it.

30:32.998 --> 30:35.834
I felt it was only right to let you know.

30:36.918 --> 30:39.338
There's a story behind this object,
isn't there?

30:41.173 --> 30:42.257
Yes, there is.

30:44.301 --> 30:46.136
Do you have a family, Chairman Kim?

30:46.887 --> 30:49.431
Yes, I have a wife and children.

30:50.599 --> 30:52.559
I had an older sister.

30:53.643 --> 30:55.354
We weren't related by blood, but…

31:02.611 --> 31:03.862
Grandma.

31:06.615 --> 31:09.159
We spent a thousand years together,
cultivating ourselves.

31:09.242 --> 31:10.744
We were like family.

31:11.370 --> 31:13.080
Be happy, Geum-ho.

31:13.163 --> 31:15.457
My lady!

31:17.376 --> 31:19.544
My lady, something terrible has happened!

31:19.628 --> 31:20.837
There are people outside--

31:20.921 --> 31:23.215
Open the gates at once!

31:23.298 --> 31:25.467
- Oh no!
- Oh my!

31:25.550 --> 31:27.010
This is the house of a traitor!

31:27.094 --> 31:29.471
Capture every single one of them!

31:35.227 --> 31:36.728
That way!

31:45.362 --> 31:46.405
Chun-sim!

32:26.611 --> 32:27.696
I can't let you in.

32:29.781 --> 32:31.992
The swordsmith is occupied at the moment.

32:32.075 --> 32:34.327
If you have business at the forge,
try somewhere else.

32:34.411 --> 32:36.246
What are you planning to do?

32:36.329 --> 32:38.748
Are you forging the Sajin Ritual Blade?

32:38.832 --> 32:40.792
What are you planning to use it for?

32:41.918 --> 32:44.337
I guess I came to the right place, then.

32:44.421 --> 32:46.298
You ignored me when I asked for your help

32:46.381 --> 32:49.050
even though I told you
I saw a miserable future for Geum-ho.

32:49.134 --> 32:51.595
But look, you chased me down like this.

32:51.678 --> 32:53.221
It's a human life.

32:53.305 --> 32:56.308
A life that Geum-ho
has to endure on her own.

32:56.808 --> 32:59.144
This isn't something you should meddle in.

32:59.227 --> 33:00.645
Don't make me laugh.

33:01.605 --> 33:03.315
It's been a thousand years.

33:03.398 --> 33:06.234
She spent a thousand years
cultivating herself and doing good deeds.

33:06.318 --> 33:08.778
Is it right for the human life
she was rewarded with

33:08.862 --> 33:12.032
to be nothing but misery and misfortune?

33:12.115 --> 33:14.201
Is that Heaven's so-called will?

33:14.284 --> 33:16.411
So making her commit a sin

33:16.495 --> 33:19.039
and undoing a thousand years
of spiritual training

33:19.122 --> 33:20.999
was the solution you came up with?

33:21.082 --> 33:25.837
Yes. Her family was branded as traitors
and condemned to live as slaves.

33:26.463 --> 33:28.048
Her husband will be beaten to death,

33:28.131 --> 33:30.425
and her children will starve,
sicken, and die.

33:30.926 --> 33:33.762
And she will grow old
having to watch it all happen.

33:34.513 --> 33:36.598
Anything would be better than that.

34:03.625 --> 34:04.709
Geum-ho.

34:08.964 --> 34:10.173
THE SAJIN RITUAL BLADE

34:11.216 --> 34:13.635
Stab him with this. You have to.

34:15.053 --> 34:17.180
- "Him"?
- I'm talking about your husband.

34:18.390 --> 34:20.433
You're not happy at all living as a human.

34:20.517 --> 34:21.643
You're miserable.

34:22.352 --> 34:24.477
If you kill the one you love
with that dagger,

34:24.560 --> 34:26.606
they say you can return
to being a nine-tailed fox.

34:29.568 --> 34:30.652
Eun-ho.

34:32.571 --> 34:36.533
I have a wish. Could you grant it for me?

34:37.534 --> 34:38.868
Of course. What is it?

34:40.412 --> 34:43.415
Promise me that you'll grant it.

34:44.541 --> 34:46.376
Very well. Go on.

34:48.295 --> 34:49.421
Don't ever

34:51.131 --> 34:53.174
appear before me again.

34:56.052 --> 34:57.304
That dagger

34:58.597 --> 35:01.099
was the last thing I gave Geum-ho.

35:02.851 --> 35:06.813
It's also one of the very few
sacred objects that can kill me.

35:13.987 --> 35:17.741
DAEHEUNG CITIZENS FC
FIRST HOME GAME OF THE SEASON

35:20.076 --> 35:21.286
- Jeez.
- Damn it.

35:22.162 --> 35:23.204
Hurry up!

35:24.831 --> 35:26.166
- Who is it?
- Good afternoon, Coach.

35:26.249 --> 35:27.542
Wait, why should I beg…

35:27.626 --> 35:29.377
K4 LEAGUE DAEHEUNG CITIZENS FC
EMBLEM CONTEST

35:29.461 --> 35:31.379
Just stay in here already! Damn it!

35:31.463 --> 35:32.464
Wait…

35:34.924 --> 35:35.925
DAEHEUNG CITIZENS FC

35:36.009 --> 35:37.802
For crying out loud.

35:42.599 --> 35:43.475
What do you want?

35:44.100 --> 35:46.269
Hey, Yong-gil!

35:47.270 --> 35:48.855
"Yong-gil"?

35:48.938 --> 35:50.732
What are you doing here? And…

35:51.316 --> 35:52.651
A black eye…

35:53.401 --> 35:54.277
"Black eye"?

35:55.987 --> 35:57.405
Where's Coach Gonzalez?

36:02.118 --> 36:03.119
Why on earth

36:04.496 --> 36:06.289
are you looking
for the national team coach?

36:06.373 --> 36:08.291
I don't know. You tell me.

36:08.792 --> 36:11.044
A bunch of weirdos showed up earlier

36:11.961 --> 36:14.255
and kept telling me
to apologize to the coach.

36:16.007 --> 36:18.968
So you're saying the coach
you need to apologize to

36:20.136 --> 36:22.639
is Gonzalez and not me?

36:22.722 --> 36:25.600
What are you talking about?
Why would I apologize to you?

36:27.644 --> 36:28.812
Where even am I?

36:32.524 --> 36:34.234
Hey, Yong-gil,

36:34.734 --> 36:37.946
it's been a while. Aren't you
even going to offer me some coffee?

36:40.281 --> 36:41.366
This little…

36:43.243 --> 36:44.869
He's lost his mind.

36:45.787 --> 36:47.747
Listen, Si-yeol.

36:49.040 --> 36:52.210
What do you think you're doing?
Is this some kind of protest?

36:52.961 --> 36:56.005
What's your problem?
Is this because I called you by name?

36:56.089 --> 36:57.132
Don't you remember?

36:57.215 --> 36:59.467
You said I could call you
by your name and not "Coach."

36:59.551 --> 37:00.593
Hey!

37:01.219 --> 37:02.721
Why are you yelling at me?

37:04.097 --> 37:05.598
Why would

37:06.349 --> 37:10.186
a fourth-division player like you
be looking for the national team coach?

37:10.812 --> 37:11.896
"Fourth division"?

37:13.523 --> 37:14.649
Me?

37:14.733 --> 37:16.651
But I'm Kang Si-yeol.

37:17.986 --> 37:21.239
I was ready to give you a second chance

37:21.322 --> 37:24.534
if you came here
and begged for forgiveness.

37:25.160 --> 37:27.620
But never mind. You're off the team!

37:29.122 --> 37:31.374
This is ridiculous.

37:31.458 --> 37:34.169
Anyone would think you were my coach.

37:34.252 --> 37:37.172
Fine, kick me off the team!

37:38.256 --> 37:41.593
Fine, you… No. You know what?

37:41.676 --> 37:45.013
I'm going to ban you
from the sport, you punk!

37:45.096 --> 37:48.433
You? Ban me? There's no way.

37:48.516 --> 37:50.185
Do whatever you want!

37:50.268 --> 37:52.854
Kick me off the team. Ban me for life.

37:52.937 --> 37:54.481
Do whatever you want!

37:55.106 --> 37:57.358
That black eye
really knocked something loose.

37:59.444 --> 38:00.570
Unbelievable!

38:00.653 --> 38:02.197
What's wrong with him?

38:02.822 --> 38:03.948
That little…

38:08.703 --> 38:11.915
- Hey, did you apologize?
- Did he say you can return to training?

38:11.998 --> 38:13.958
You didn't cause more trouble, did you?

38:17.420 --> 38:18.588
Be honest with me.

38:19.923 --> 38:21.424
Is this a hidden camera prank?

38:22.884 --> 38:23.802
What?

38:25.470 --> 38:26.513
This is for YouTube, right?

38:27.806 --> 38:29.015
Whose channel is it?

38:29.098 --> 38:32.185
You shouldn't be doing this
just for views. I'm Kang Si-yeol.

38:34.813 --> 38:35.855
What's with him today?

38:38.358 --> 38:39.943
You can't do this.

38:40.026 --> 38:42.821
Even if you're desperate for views,
you need to ask first.

38:56.376 --> 38:58.002
- I'm borrowing this.
- Wait…

38:59.671 --> 39:01.548
- What…
- What's going on?

39:11.015 --> 39:12.392
It wasn't just the cameras.

39:12.475 --> 39:15.186
The whole security system
went down briefly.

39:16.396 --> 39:19.023
Do you have any idea
what might have happened?

39:19.107 --> 39:20.900
It doesn't make any sense, sir.

39:20.984 --> 39:23.903
Everything was normal
during our last patrol.

39:24.571 --> 39:26.030
Looks like your memory was erased.

39:27.031 --> 39:28.283
Pardon?

39:28.366 --> 39:31.494
You really didn't notice anything unusual?

39:32.662 --> 39:34.539
No, ma'am. We patrol in pairs--

39:34.622 --> 39:36.332
Look me in the eye.

39:38.084 --> 39:40.670
Are you sure you didn't notice
anything unusual?

39:41.629 --> 39:43.631
Well…

39:44.966 --> 39:46.593
Actually, there was someone.

39:48.845 --> 39:50.179
It was a man.

39:50.263 --> 39:52.807
- Sir!
- Stay out of this.

39:54.642 --> 39:55.685
A man?

39:56.853 --> 39:57.896
Was he alone?

39:58.396 --> 40:03.234
Yes. I tried to stop him
and asked how he got in--

40:17.832 --> 40:19.250
He's under a binding spell.

40:35.266 --> 40:39.604
I didn't realize there were still humans
who could use techniques like that.

40:39.687 --> 40:40.647
A human?

40:42.231 --> 40:43.816
Can a human do such a thing?

40:44.776 --> 40:46.527
It's not something just anyone can do.

40:47.320 --> 40:50.448
A mere human
mimicking the powers of a deity

40:50.949 --> 40:53.576
will pay a steep price.

40:55.119 --> 40:58.831
Why would someone like that
need the wooden-handled dagger?

41:01.042 --> 41:02.126
Could they be…

41:03.503 --> 41:06.172
trying to harm you?

41:08.299 --> 41:11.678
Do you really think a human
who's learned a few cheap tricks like this

41:11.761 --> 41:13.596
could actually harm me?

41:15.515 --> 41:19.018
Sure, I'd die if I were stabbed.
But how would he even do that?

41:19.519 --> 41:21.312
I'd like to see him try.

41:21.396 --> 41:22.480
That's a relief then.

41:23.648 --> 41:24.941
So what should we do?

41:26.317 --> 41:27.860
I'm not sure.

41:29.278 --> 41:32.198
But let me take a look at him first.

41:38.955 --> 41:41.374
ADVANCING CORRECTIONS FOR THE FUTURE

41:41.457 --> 41:43.876
HUMAN-CENTERED CORRECTIONS
MINISTRY OF JUSTICE

42:04.188 --> 42:05.398
It's been a while.

42:06.899 --> 42:08.317
Seeing you out here,

42:09.068 --> 42:10.903
you look like a different person.

42:13.614 --> 42:16.868
TWO YEARS AGO

42:24.417 --> 42:27.045
There's no need to search
this cell so thoroughly.

42:27.587 --> 42:30.214
- Excuse me?
- Jeez, come with me.

42:36.637 --> 42:38.431
Inmate 478, anything to report?

42:45.897 --> 42:49.275
Inmate 133 has
cigarettes stashed in his cell.

42:49.358 --> 42:52.070
Inmate 2759 is making flower cards
out of cardboard.

42:52.153 --> 42:54.739
And as for Inmate 1614…

42:57.533 --> 42:59.118
You little piece of shit!

42:59.202 --> 43:01.954
- You little bastard!
- Why did this jerk end up in our cell?

43:02.038 --> 43:02.955
Damn it!

43:08.294 --> 43:09.712
You crazy bastard.

43:09.796 --> 43:12.215
Hey, I heard your father disowned you.

43:12.882 --> 43:14.884
You're nothing now, you piece of shit.

43:17.011 --> 43:19.388
Hey, look at me when I'm talking to you.

43:19.472 --> 43:22.016
- I should poke your eyes out!
- That's enough.

43:23.726 --> 43:25.812
What did you just say, old man?

43:26.562 --> 43:30.191
Hey, you just got here,
so you clearly don't know how things work.

43:30.274 --> 43:33.945
- Mind your own damn business.
- I said, that's enough.

43:36.739 --> 43:38.950
I've got business with this guy.

43:40.785 --> 43:42.328
Is he out of his mind?

43:45.414 --> 43:46.541
What's going on?

43:51.629 --> 43:52.713
What the…

44:01.848 --> 44:03.057
We need to talk.

44:03.141 --> 44:04.684
Who the hell are you?

44:05.393 --> 44:08.354
It's a bit cramped in here.
Why don't we go for a walk?

44:31.169 --> 44:33.713
So you're not human either?

44:35.131 --> 44:36.007
I'm human.

44:37.717 --> 44:40.303
That doesn't make sense. How…

44:40.386 --> 44:41.929
How could a human…

44:42.555 --> 44:45.141
Why wouldn't a human
be able to do what a mere fox can do?

44:45.224 --> 44:47.143
It's just a little tricky, that's all.

44:53.524 --> 44:54.609
Take this.

44:55.443 --> 44:56.611
What is it?

44:57.278 --> 44:58.487
A warding sigil.

44:58.988 --> 45:00.823
It's a talisman to ward off evil.

45:01.490 --> 45:03.451
As long as you have this on you,

45:03.534 --> 45:06.913
the nine-tailed fox's spell
won't affect you.

45:33.105 --> 45:35.650
No need to thank me.

45:37.360 --> 45:38.653
But when you get out,

45:39.362 --> 45:40.947
let's do a job together.

45:57.255 --> 45:58.339
Jeez.

45:59.173 --> 46:01.008
Where are we going?

46:01.092 --> 46:02.426
I told you before.

46:02.510 --> 46:05.179
I said let's do a job together
once you get out.

46:05.930 --> 46:07.640
What exactly is this "job"?

46:08.307 --> 46:09.809
It's nothing difficult.

46:11.352 --> 46:13.187
You just need to act as bait.

46:14.146 --> 46:16.065
- What?
- Starting now,

46:17.566 --> 46:19.485
I'm going on a fox hunt.

46:26.826 --> 46:33.457
JOSEON-ERA INK-WASH PAINTING
DEPICTING COMMERCIAL ACTIVITY

46:34.583 --> 46:36.085
You there, painter.

46:36.627 --> 46:38.796
I was thinking of commissioning something.

46:39.547 --> 46:43.384
I don't have anything to offer,
but I can buy you a drink.

46:48.472 --> 46:52.059
I heard someone took the dagger
from over there last night.

46:52.727 --> 46:54.895
Could you do a quick sketch of him for me?

47:09.368 --> 47:11.412
Why isn't Woo-seok picking up?

47:35.644 --> 47:37.313
I don't think you're a resident here.

47:38.481 --> 47:40.733
Oh, it's me.

47:41.942 --> 47:44.695
I've never seen you before.
Which unit are you visiting?

47:46.030 --> 47:47.615
- Pardon?
- What?

47:47.698 --> 47:49.408
Come on now.

47:58.542 --> 47:59.627
What?

48:09.428 --> 48:10.304
Who are you?

48:10.388 --> 48:13.182
I'm sorry. I thought this was my home.

48:15.351 --> 48:18.270
Wait, this is my home.

48:18.354 --> 48:19.647
What a weirdo.

48:20.356 --> 48:21.273
Oh my goodness!

48:21.357 --> 48:22.441
- Wait.
- What are you doing?

48:22.525 --> 48:24.068
Who are you? Why are you in my--

48:24.151 --> 48:26.195
What is wrong with you? Are you crazy?

48:26.278 --> 48:27.488
Excuse me.

48:27.571 --> 48:29.365
- Sir, this woman--
- Sir, this man--

48:29.448 --> 48:31.492
This guy's really asking for trouble.

48:32.159 --> 48:34.578
- Who are you?
- What's wrong with you?

48:34.662 --> 48:37.081
Don't you recognize me?

48:38.207 --> 48:40.251
How on earth would I know who you are?

48:40.334 --> 48:42.128
- Come on, get out.
- Wait a second!

48:42.211 --> 48:43.671
That's enough. Out!

48:43.754 --> 48:45.089
Wait…

48:46.507 --> 48:48.717
Oh my goodness!

48:49.385 --> 48:50.553
What's going on?

48:50.636 --> 48:51.512
Excuse me!

48:51.595 --> 48:52.972
- This is my home.
- Do something!

48:53.055 --> 48:54.306
- Yes, ma'am.
- My gosh!

48:54.390 --> 48:56.016
- Excuse me.
- This really is my home.

48:56.100 --> 48:57.184
He's just…

48:57.852 --> 48:58.894
This isn't possible.

48:58.978 --> 49:00.229
What's wrong with him? Hey!

49:00.855 --> 49:02.523
- Are you out of your mind?
- Oh my!

49:02.606 --> 49:04.608
No, this seriously isn't possible.

49:04.692 --> 49:07.069
Come on! I told you to get out!

49:07.862 --> 49:09.572
I'm very sorry about this.

49:09.655 --> 49:11.198
Come on, let's go!

49:24.920 --> 49:27.131
What is all this?

49:27.756 --> 49:28.883
It's a trap.

49:29.467 --> 49:31.719
I told you, I'm going on a fox hunt.

49:32.428 --> 49:34.889
You can catch a nine-tailed fox with this?

49:34.972 --> 49:37.224
All you have to do is set the right bait.

49:38.517 --> 49:40.060
A wicked creature like that

49:40.144 --> 49:43.481
can never escape
once it's trapped in this sacred rope.

49:48.277 --> 49:50.112
Why are you doing all this?

49:51.238 --> 49:53.949
Do you have a grudge
against the nine-tailed fox too?

49:55.576 --> 49:58.287
A hunter doesn't hunt
because of a personal grudge.

50:35.199 --> 50:36.492
What are you doing?

50:37.660 --> 50:40.579
Shut your mouth and stay still.
We don't want to jinx it.

51:05.563 --> 51:06.564
What is this?

51:21.537 --> 51:22.538
You.

51:23.747 --> 51:26.417
Food's here. Go on and stuff your face!

51:36.927 --> 51:37.886
What is that?

51:38.470 --> 51:41.557
It's the vengeful spirit
of a starved wild dog.

51:42.641 --> 51:43.726
What?

51:45.185 --> 51:46.854
- Roll up your sleeve.
- Pardon?

51:48.939 --> 51:51.150
- Are you crazy? What are you doing?
- Roll it up.

51:52.401 --> 51:53.527
Damn it.

51:57.072 --> 51:58.073
Stay still.

52:04.830 --> 52:08.792
That dog needs to pick up
the fox scent all over you.

52:08.876 --> 52:11.962
The protective talisman you have
masks the fox's scent.

52:13.088 --> 52:16.592
If you're done stuffing your face,
it's time to earn your keep.

52:16.675 --> 52:19.803
This guy is under the fox's spell.

52:20.763 --> 52:23.682
Don't move a muscle
unless you want to be torn to pieces.

52:26.226 --> 52:27.603
Here.

52:28.562 --> 52:33.317
Now, go and find out where that fox is.

52:55.923 --> 52:58.884
SOLLENFORD AIRPORT, LONDON, UK

53:07.434 --> 53:09.478
ONLY WOO-SEOK!

53:09.561 --> 53:10.729
LOVE YOU FOREVER
WOO-SEOK

53:18.529 --> 53:19.405
Woo-seok.

53:22.366 --> 53:23.534
Dad?

53:24.952 --> 53:26.704
Why are you here, Dad?

53:27.371 --> 53:28.414
What do you mean?

53:30.374 --> 53:32.084
Where else would I be?

53:35.921 --> 53:37.005
I see.

53:38.006 --> 53:38.882
Right.

53:38.966 --> 53:41.760
Wait, listen to me. I'm not some weirdo.

53:42.720 --> 53:45.013
I'm telling you that really is my home.

53:45.097 --> 53:47.015
Hey, wait…

53:47.516 --> 53:50.394
But do you seriously not know me?
Don't you watch soccer?

53:50.477 --> 53:53.147
Don't you know Kang Si-yeol,
the world's best athlete?

53:55.315 --> 53:58.277
What did you do
to get yourself thrown in here already?

53:58.360 --> 53:59.361
You!

53:59.445 --> 54:01.363
Perfect timing. Hold on a moment.

54:03.073 --> 54:04.700
- Hey, you.
- Yes?

54:19.840 --> 54:21.425
Find someone who looks like this.

54:21.508 --> 54:23.510
Use any means necessary.

54:25.220 --> 54:26.180
Yes, ma'am.

54:44.948 --> 54:46.867
Do you understand what's going on now?

54:48.410 --> 54:49.745
Damn it.

54:52.498 --> 54:54.792
What did you do to me?

54:55.834 --> 54:57.377
I guess not yet.

54:59.671 --> 55:02.007
All right. I'll fill you in now.

55:04.510 --> 55:07.888
I switched your fates.

55:10.641 --> 55:11.767
What?

55:11.850 --> 55:15.479
So, in this world,
the Kang Si-yeol you knew is gone.

55:15.979 --> 55:17.564
Because your fate has changed.

55:17.648 --> 55:19.900
Just tell me what's going on!

55:19.983 --> 55:25.280
What does no one recognizing me
have to do with Woo-seok's wish?

55:25.364 --> 55:26.573
And what happened to my house?

55:26.657 --> 55:29.868
That's the price you paid
for your friend's wish.

55:31.870 --> 55:35.707
For every rise, there must be a fall.

55:36.375 --> 55:38.585
For someone to take the throne,

55:38.669 --> 55:40.838
someone else
must be stripped of their crown.

55:41.880 --> 55:43.257
That's the law of the world.

55:43.340 --> 55:45.300
Not even I can change that.

55:47.344 --> 55:48.345
So,

55:49.304 --> 55:51.098
when you say
our fates have been switched…

55:51.181 --> 55:54.059
Since someone became
a world-class soccer player,

55:55.727 --> 55:59.439
someone else had to step down.

56:01.149 --> 56:03.318
That's the only way
to maintain the balance.

56:18.959 --> 56:19.877
Then…

56:22.462 --> 56:24.089
it wasn't just a dream?

56:24.172 --> 56:25.465
The past was rewritten.

56:26.258 --> 56:28.093
Naturally, the present followed suit.

56:28.802 --> 56:29.887
No way in hell.

56:30.554 --> 56:32.806
So I really am a fourth-division player?

56:33.348 --> 56:34.516
Are you kidding me? You…

56:36.226 --> 56:37.311
What's the problem?

56:37.394 --> 56:39.771
I made your friend a world-class player

56:39.855 --> 56:42.983
who plays in the European leagues
and for the national team.

56:43.066 --> 56:45.986
Isn't that enough?
That's what you both wished for.

56:46.612 --> 56:49.907
"Enough"? The hell it is! I'm literally…

56:58.498 --> 57:01.919
Whatever. Just put everything back
the way it was. Right now.

57:03.295 --> 57:05.756
- I'm afraid I can't do that.
- Why the hell not?

57:06.924 --> 57:10.552
Because you have nothing left
to pay for a wish.

57:10.636 --> 57:14.056
You have no money,
and the life you built is gone.

57:14.765 --> 57:15.766
Then…

57:17.434 --> 57:19.561
I have to keep living like this?

57:21.229 --> 57:24.483
Well, there is a way.

57:25.651 --> 57:26.526
What is it?

57:35.118 --> 57:36.078
What's going on?

57:36.161 --> 57:39.247
This is my place in London.

57:41.083 --> 57:42.167
Gosh.

57:46.088 --> 57:48.715
This is our house? For real?

57:49.341 --> 57:51.969
- Woo-seok.
- Oh gosh.

57:52.052 --> 57:53.929
What has he been going on about?

57:54.012 --> 57:55.305
Of course this is our house.

58:20.914 --> 58:22.290
It's simple.

58:22.916 --> 58:26.712
All your friend needs to do
is make a wish, just like you did.

58:26.795 --> 58:28.922
A wish to switch your fates back.

58:29.923 --> 58:30.799
What?

58:31.425 --> 58:32.426
Woo-seok.

58:33.176 --> 58:34.553
Have you thought about it?

58:36.930 --> 58:38.557
About what?

58:38.640 --> 58:41.018
Your transfer. Where do you want to go?

58:41.768 --> 58:44.855
They said they'll match
any contract terms we want.

58:45.689 --> 58:46.690
So,

58:47.774 --> 58:49.735
you just have to make the final call.

59:06.168 --> 59:07.127
I can go…

59:09.087 --> 59:10.881
anywhere I want?

59:12.090 --> 59:14.676
Of course, you're Hyeon Woo-seok.

59:17.512 --> 59:18.847
But I wonder

59:19.598 --> 59:21.975
if your friend
would actually make that wish?

59:22.059 --> 59:23.435
For your sake?

59:25.854 --> 59:30.150
He finally has the life
he's always dreamed of.

59:30.233 --> 59:32.360
He's only just started living it.

59:45.999 --> 59:47.084
Why…

59:49.961 --> 59:51.379
are you doing this to me?

59:52.297 --> 59:56.134
I can't stand humans
who get cocky with me.

59:57.385 --> 59:59.179
To be my client,

59:59.971 --> 01:00:02.390
I needed to teach you some manners first.

01:00:03.642 --> 01:00:04.976
That's it?

01:00:05.977 --> 01:00:10.315
Do you think it's okay
to toy with people's lives like this?

01:00:10.816 --> 01:00:12.359
Why are you getting so worked up?

01:00:13.068 --> 01:00:15.946
Everything can be easily fixed
if your friend makes the wish.

01:00:18.156 --> 01:00:21.451
What's wrong?
You don't trust your friend either?

01:00:26.873 --> 01:00:28.583
Actually, I'm curious too.

01:00:29.709 --> 01:00:33.338
Let's see how your friend
decides to play this.

01:01:16.840 --> 01:01:19.759
NO TAIL TO TELL

01:01:19.843 --> 01:01:22.929
Si-yeol, just one month.
Let's switch back in a month.

01:01:23.013 --> 01:01:24.639
Hyeon Woo-seok! Oh, come on!

01:01:24.723 --> 01:01:26.224
No, no.

01:01:26.308 --> 01:01:28.476
Are you saying
I have to keep living like this?

01:01:28.560 --> 01:01:31.855
I'm going to burn this place down!
Put me down!

01:01:31.938 --> 01:01:34.149
I can't live like that. I won't, damn it!

01:01:34.232 --> 01:01:35.400
Have you learned your lesson?

01:01:35.483 --> 01:01:38.528
Put me back! Please.

01:01:38.612 --> 01:01:41.698
Well, that should do it.
I guess I've tamed you enough.

01:01:41.781 --> 01:01:42.741
Shall we end this here?

01:01:42.824 --> 01:01:44.451
Is it good?

01:01:44.534 --> 01:01:45.577
Where to?

01:01:45.660 --> 01:01:47.412
I'm sorry. I thought this was a taxi.

01:01:47.495 --> 01:01:49.998
You have the wish-granting
business card, don't you?

01:01:50.081 --> 01:01:52.375
I have some business with that fox.

01:01:52.876 --> 01:01:54.169
Get up, Kang Si-yeol.

01:01:56.588 --> 01:01:58.632
Subtitle translation by Susanna Kim
